  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;be a line which is normal to the curve <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;at a point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;on the curve. If the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;lies on the line <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;is origin, then the area of the triangle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;is equal to _____.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "13",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The given curve is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/186c0d68-a71b-481b-8805-541414015d9e-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 197px;\" /></p><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>, then normal at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Since this normal passes through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Q</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mfenced><mrow><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Also&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>h</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now area of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8710;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>P</mi><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\"><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>6</mn></mtd><mtd><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>13</mn></math></p>",
